(Section 6: Mechanical seal replacement \(seal swap\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(WARNING: Lock out the pump before service.) Tj T*
(Lock out and tag out the pump motor before any service work.) Tj T*
(Tools: 13 mm wrench, seal kit SK-450, drain pan, clean rag.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Close the suction valve and the discharge valve.) Tj T*
(2. Drain the casing through the drain plug at the bottom \(Figure 7\).) Tj T*
(3. Remove the four casing bolts and slide the motor and impeller back.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
5 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 8 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Contents 4 0 R /Resources << /Font << /F1 1 0 R >> >> >>
endobj
6 0 obj
<< /Length 475 >>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 56 770 Td
(4. Remove the old seal and clean the shaft sleeve with a clean rag.) Tj T*
(5. Install the new seal from kit SK-450. Do not touch the seal faces.) Tj T*
(6. Reassemble, refill, open both valves, and run for 10 minutes while you check for) Tj T*
(   leaks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Figure 7: the drain plug is the 13 mm hex plug at the lowest point of the casing.) Tj T*
(After a seal replacement, do a leak check again after 7 days of running.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
